text: ['Defender\\nWhen Wall of Omens enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'Destroy target nonartifact creature.', 'Draw three cards.', 'Flash\\nFlying\\nWhen Spellstutter Sprite enters the battlefield, counter target spell with mana value X or less, where X is the number of Faeries you control.', 'Flying\\nWhen Squadron Hawk enters the battlefield, you may search your library for up to three cards named Squadron Hawk, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Lifelink', 'Multikicker {2} (You may pay an additional {2} any number of times as you cast this spell.)\\nEverflowing Chalice enters the battlefield with a charge counter on it for each time it was kicked.\\n{T}: Add {C} for each charge counter on Everflowing Chalice.', 'Savage Lands enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}, {R}, or {G}.', 'Search your library for up to two basic land cards, reveal those cards, put one onto the battlefield tapped and the other into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Teetering Peaks enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Teetering Peaks enters the battlefield, target creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn.\\n{T}: Add {R}.', 'When Contagion Clasp enters the battlefield, put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.\\n{4}, {T}: Proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', 'When you cast this spell, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nAnnihilator 2 (Whenever this creature attacks, defending player sacrifices two permanents.)']
flavor: ['"Brute force can sometimes kick down a locked door, but knowledge is a skeleton key."', '"I search for a vision of Zendikar that does not include the Eldrazi."\\n—Expedition journal entry', 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', 'Having flesh is increasingly a liability on Mirrodin.', 'Jund is a world as cruel as those who call it home. Their brutal struggles scar the land even as it carves them in its image, a vicious circle spiraling out of control.', 'Rhox monks are dedicated to spiritual growth and learning, and most bear the sigils of many students. However, they do not gladly suffer fools or those who disagree with their carefully wrought dogma.']
